WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:03.033
- I think, it has to be probably
when I was in eighth grade.

00:00:03.960 --> 00:00:05.070
A girl in my class told me

00:00:05.070 --> 00:00:07.380
I was one of the two
ugliest boys in the school.

00:00:07.380 --> 00:00:08.213
That's been

00:00:10.470 --> 00:00:13.710
well over 40 years since
I was in eighth grade.

00:00:13.710 --> 00:00:15.694
And to be carrying it still now

00:00:15.694 --> 00:00:19.260
into the fifth decade is crazy.

00:00:19.260 --> 00:00:23.520
Any time I think I might be
dressed well or look good,

00:00:23.520 --> 00:00:25.140
that does come back and haunt me

00:00:25.140 --> 00:00:25.973
and just says, well,

00:00:25.973 --> 00:00:28.230
you're one of the two
ugliest boys in our class.

00:00:29.190 --> 00:00:31.110
- I guess, I was stupid.

00:00:31.110 --> 00:00:32.223
Yeah, just homework.

00:00:33.764 --> 00:00:37.641
Homework and little things
like dropping glass.

00:00:37.641 --> 00:00:38.474
Me and my dad,

00:00:38.474 --> 00:00:40.170
don't really have that good
of relationship right now,

00:00:40.170 --> 00:00:42.697
because of the way he's talked
to me when I was little.

00:00:42.697 --> 00:00:45.150
But I was stuck feeling
stupid for a long time.

00:00:45.150 --> 00:00:46.770
I feel like I was like playing myself down

00:00:46.770 --> 00:00:48.090
for a lot of situations,

00:00:48.090 --> 00:00:49.980
because what my dad
said to me in the past.

00:00:49.980 --> 00:00:53.313
So, it's just like, I don't know. Yeah.

00:00:54.150 --> 00:00:54.983
- Okay.

00:00:54.983 --> 00:00:56.550
So, the most painful thing I've been told

00:00:56.550 --> 00:00:57.533
was by my mother

00:00:57.533 --> 00:01:02.533
when she essentially blamed
me for my grandmother's death.

00:01:02.910 --> 00:01:06.240
We were traveling, my
grandmother's sick at home,

00:01:06.240 --> 00:01:09.440
and then she told me, because
I had said a swear word,

00:01:09.440 --> 00:01:11.580
it was just damn, the word was damn.

00:01:11.580 --> 00:01:13.470
And then, the next day, my
grandmother had passed away.

00:01:13.470 --> 00:01:14.730
She's like, "Because you said that,

00:01:14.730 --> 00:01:16.620
your grandmother passed away."

00:01:16.620 --> 00:01:18.960
I still hold that against her to this day.

00:01:18.960 --> 00:01:21.600
I can't see my mom the
same because of that.

00:01:21.600 --> 00:01:23.987
And I hold incredible guilt

00:01:23.987 --> 00:01:26.700
surrounding my grandmother's death.

00:01:26.700 --> 00:01:27.630
- [Thoraya] Do you think you'll ever

00:01:27.630 --> 00:01:28.803
find healing from it?

00:01:30.000 --> 00:01:32.190
- No. I would have to like...

00:01:32.190 --> 00:01:34.830
Unless my grandmother could
come back from the dead herself

00:01:34.830 --> 00:01:37.410
to tell me like, it's not your fault,

00:01:37.410 --> 00:01:39.360
I don't think I could ever get over it.

00:01:41.010 --> 00:01:42.273
- So, when I was a child,

00:01:43.916 --> 00:01:45.333
I had a really,

00:01:47.102 --> 00:01:48.702
it was a very violent childhood.

00:01:49.740 --> 00:01:51.850
And when I was

00:01:52.890 --> 00:01:54.570
about 18 years old,

00:01:54.570 --> 00:01:56.270
I got kicked out of my mom's house

00:01:57.180 --> 00:01:58.899
and one of the things that she told me

00:01:58.899 --> 00:02:02.520
was to get the (censored)
out of her house.

00:02:02.520 --> 00:02:06.790
And she called me a piece of (censored)

00:02:09.787 --> 00:02:12.420
I held onto that for

00:02:12.420 --> 00:02:14.403
the last 15 years almost.

00:02:15.420 --> 00:02:20.117
I've stemmed in all kinds of
things, abandonment issues,

00:02:21.420 --> 00:02:23.790
thinking that I was a piece of (censored)

00:02:23.790 --> 00:02:27.750
And essentially, letting
that mold a huge part

00:02:27.750 --> 00:02:30.650
of who I had become in my early 20s

00:02:30.650 --> 00:02:34.323
and basically until
recently, to be honest.

00:02:36.300 --> 00:02:38.880
So, yeah, I think, that
was the hardest thing

00:02:38.880 --> 00:02:41.673
that I've ever heard
was from my own mother.

00:02:43.710 --> 00:02:45.847
- It was my mom telling me,

00:02:45.847 --> 00:02:47.597
"How could I ever be proud of you?"

00:02:49.140 --> 00:02:51.510
When I came out to her.

00:02:51.510 --> 00:02:53.350
And that always sticks in my

00:02:54.540 --> 00:02:55.630
psyche (laughs) that

00:02:56.640 --> 00:02:58.440
just not being able to like,

00:02:58.440 --> 00:02:59.557
my mom asking me,

00:02:59.557 --> 00:03:02.820
"How could I ever be proud of
you when you're not straight?"

00:03:02.820 --> 00:03:04.713
Whatever. So, yeah.

00:03:06.390 --> 00:03:10.650
- It was, I think, my
dad was really mad at me

00:03:10.650 --> 00:03:13.170
and he was mocking me,

00:03:13.170 --> 00:03:17.160
because a year earlier,
I tried to kill myself

00:03:17.160 --> 00:03:20.040
and he was making fun of that.

00:03:20.040 --> 00:03:20.873
He said,

00:03:21.757 --> 00:03:24.607
"Oh at least I'm not the kid
that tried to kill himself."

00:03:26.100 --> 00:03:28.421
- Your dad ain't never cared about you

00:03:28.421 --> 00:03:31.020
and he don't give a (censored) about you.

00:03:31.020 --> 00:03:33.780
I just started talking back to my dad now.

00:03:33.780 --> 00:03:35.610
Things have been good.

00:03:35.610 --> 00:03:36.720
When I speak to him now though,

00:03:36.720 --> 00:03:40.140
he'd be the only one that
seemed like listen for real.

00:03:40.140 --> 00:03:41.820
And it's like you live in a world

00:03:41.820 --> 00:03:43.560
where everybody has their own perspective

00:03:43.560 --> 00:03:46.320
and nobody wants to get
to know anybody else's.

00:03:46.320 --> 00:03:48.839
But when I talk to him, I feel that.

00:03:48.839 --> 00:03:51.600
And he give me that idea
that he really do care

00:03:51.600 --> 00:03:54.510
about what I gotta think about
and that we not so different.

00:03:54.510 --> 00:03:55.607
And it's crazier too,

00:03:55.607 --> 00:03:57.750
'cause me and my dad got the same name,

00:03:57.750 --> 00:03:59.430
so it make me feel

00:03:59.430 --> 00:04:02.230
like I do got somebody on
this earth that understand me.

00:04:03.510 --> 00:04:06.360
- The most painful thing I was told

00:04:06.360 --> 00:04:08.760
was when my dad woke me up

00:04:08.760 --> 00:04:11.223
and told me that my nana had passed away.

00:04:12.510 --> 00:04:13.710
Yeah. (chuckles)

00:04:13.710 --> 00:04:15.870
Every day, I find moments where I'm like,

00:04:15.870 --> 00:04:17.880
oh, I wish I could just call her

00:04:17.880 --> 00:04:22.241
or let her know what's new in my life.

00:04:22.241 --> 00:04:24.760
I very much leaned on her when I was

00:04:25.980 --> 00:04:27.360
younger.

00:04:27.360 --> 00:04:29.190
My mom worked a lot.

00:04:29.190 --> 00:04:30.150
She was a young mom,

00:04:30.150 --> 00:04:32.520
so she took care of us for the most part.

00:04:32.520 --> 00:04:37.110
I would just say she embodied sunshine.

00:04:37.110 --> 00:04:40.110
Any room she walked in, if
it was dark, it was light.

00:04:40.110 --> 00:04:41.940
She had this laugh that anytime

00:04:41.940 --> 00:04:43.980
you would hear it, was
like a cackle. (laughs)

00:04:43.980 --> 00:04:45.690
It was annoying a little bit,

00:04:45.690 --> 00:04:47.400
but really, really funny.

00:04:47.400 --> 00:04:51.900
And you couldn't help, but laugh as well.

00:04:51.900 --> 00:04:53.340
She's just very special.

00:04:53.340 --> 00:04:54.360
Thank you for asking.

00:04:54.360 --> 00:04:57.270
It feels good to open up a little bit,

00:04:57.270 --> 00:04:59.220
'cause I don't talk about it often,

00:04:59.220 --> 00:05:00.570
but I don't know,

00:05:00.570 --> 00:05:03.960
sharing just a part of her in
my day feels good. (chuckles)

00:05:03.960 --> 00:05:05.040
So, thank you.
- Yeah.

00:05:05.040 --> 00:05:06.270
What was your name?

00:05:06.270 --> 00:05:07.650
- Cheryl.
- Okay.

00:05:07.650 --> 00:05:10.530
- My name is Cheryl.
Cheryl too. (chuckles)

00:05:10.530 --> 00:05:13.763
- The first thing comes
from my mind is when

00:05:15.092 --> 00:05:20.092
someone I know told me that
my brother is better than me

00:05:20.337 --> 00:05:22.020
and a lot of stuff.

00:05:22.020 --> 00:05:26.370
When I'm with my brother, I
feel like I'm not there at all.

00:05:26.370 --> 00:05:27.426
- [Thoraya] When you're with your brother,

00:05:27.426 --> 00:05:28.259
- Uh-huh.
- with a lot of people,

00:05:28.259 --> 00:05:29.310
you don't show your personality?

00:05:29.310 --> 00:05:32.497
- Yeah, because my brother
is like show up to everyone

00:05:32.497 --> 00:05:34.677
- Mm.
- and I'm like in the back.

00:05:34.677 --> 00:05:38.879
And the most painful thing
was when I enter to a room

00:05:38.879 --> 00:05:43.140
and someone says like,
where's your brother?

00:05:43.140 --> 00:05:46.470
And you, why are you
here? Something like that.

00:05:46.470 --> 00:05:49.410
And that was like a
shock to me. (chuckles)

00:05:49.410 --> 00:05:51.510
He doesn't know that I feel

00:05:51.510 --> 00:05:56.510
like I can't show me when I'm with him.

00:05:56.790 --> 00:05:57.623
- [Thoraya] You've never told him?

00:05:57.623 --> 00:05:59.400
- No, no.

00:05:59.400 --> 00:06:00.567
- [Thoraya] Does the way you feel

00:06:00.567 --> 00:06:03.513
and the things you were told,
- Mm-hmm, mm-hmm.

00:06:03.513 --> 00:06:06.390
- [Thoraya] does it change how you feel

00:06:06.390 --> 00:06:07.690
about your brother at all?

00:06:09.727 --> 00:06:13.563
- Five years ago, yes. Now, no.

00:06:14.550 --> 00:06:18.810
I go to therapy, so I
can change that feeling,

00:06:18.810 --> 00:06:20.610
because it was a very bad feeling,

00:06:20.610 --> 00:06:23.790
because my brother
doesn't have that fault.

00:06:23.790 --> 00:06:25.710
- Mm-hmm.
- That what I...

00:06:25.710 --> 00:06:29.580
I was free. So, no, no, no, no, no.

00:06:29.580 --> 00:06:31.500
I love him. (chuckles) Yeah.

00:06:31.500 --> 00:06:33.030
- Oh, the first time someone told me

00:06:33.030 --> 00:06:35.610
me and my sister didn't
look alike, I guess.

00:06:35.610 --> 00:06:38.190
'cause that's my favorite
person in the entire world.

00:06:38.190 --> 00:06:42.090
So, telling us that we
didn't look alike was harsh.

00:06:42.090 --> 00:06:46.890
Like my own blood, my own
person was not looking like me.

00:06:46.890 --> 00:06:48.870
We didn't act alike at the
time. So, it was weird.

00:06:48.870 --> 00:06:51.386
It hurt a lot. (laughs)

00:06:51.386 --> 00:06:53.010
(interviewee chuckles)

00:06:53.010 --> 00:06:55.665
They're my favorite person
on this entire planet.

00:06:55.665 --> 00:06:58.165
(piano music)

00:07:00.420 --> 00:07:05.420
- I think, in my first relationship,
I was told things like,

00:07:05.634 --> 00:07:08.370
"God, you can't really do
anything by yourself, can you?"

00:07:08.370 --> 00:07:10.647
Or like, "How would you
survive without me?"

00:07:11.490 --> 00:07:12.870
Just really demeaning things

00:07:12.870 --> 00:07:16.500
that made me feel like I
couldn't be my own person.

00:07:16.500 --> 00:07:19.650
So, it really sunk into me for a long time

00:07:19.650 --> 00:07:23.130
that I couldn't be by myself
and I couldn't be my own person

00:07:23.130 --> 00:07:26.910
and I needed someone to help
me with everything in my life.

00:07:26.910 --> 00:07:28.800
And I knew deep down
that that wasn't true,

00:07:28.800 --> 00:07:31.620
because I'd always been
very independent as a kid,

00:07:31.620 --> 00:07:36.150
but that person just sucked
my entire soul into theirs

00:07:36.150 --> 00:07:38.460
and devoured it and spit it back out.

00:07:38.460 --> 00:07:42.690
And it took a long time to unlearn that

00:07:42.690 --> 00:07:44.790
and realize that that's not true.

00:07:44.790 --> 00:07:46.590
And that was their insecurity

00:07:46.590 --> 00:07:48.840
of knowing that if I realized

00:07:48.840 --> 00:07:51.360
that I could do anything
myself, I would leave.

00:07:51.360 --> 00:07:56.360
Now, I live fully nomadically in my van.

00:07:57.210 --> 00:07:58.650
I've been doing it for three years

00:07:58.650 --> 00:08:01.860
and it's been my dream since
before I met that person.

00:08:01.860 --> 00:08:03.240
And I do everything by myself,

00:08:03.240 --> 00:08:05.940
and I feel like completely
confident in that fact.

00:08:05.940 --> 00:08:07.840
And it's a really beautiful

00:08:09.870 --> 00:08:12.570
circle moment, full circle moment.

00:08:12.570 --> 00:08:14.490
- So, I've been complimented a lot.

00:08:14.490 --> 00:08:15.390
This is a compliment,

00:08:15.390 --> 00:08:20.390
but it's painful to me that
I'm such a very good listener

00:08:20.520 --> 00:08:22.710
and that I listen to people well.

00:08:22.710 --> 00:08:26.280
But I take it as a painful thing to hear,

00:08:26.280 --> 00:08:29.070
because I feel like I don't
share my feelings enough

00:08:29.070 --> 00:08:30.890
and I'm very...

00:08:31.890 --> 00:08:33.930
I don't speak a lot to other people,

00:08:33.930 --> 00:08:35.910
and so I feel like people never hear me.

00:08:35.910 --> 00:08:37.080
So, I feel like when I speak,

00:08:37.080 --> 00:08:39.153
they don't listen as much as I do.

00:08:40.320 --> 00:08:42.695
- Because of my situation,
I can't really travel.

00:08:42.695 --> 00:08:46.083
So, when my family travels out,

00:08:47.910 --> 00:08:50.556
they express to me that they
have to disconnect from me,

00:08:50.556 --> 00:08:53.733
forget that I'm here so
they can enjoy themselves.

00:08:55.080 --> 00:08:57.930
- I think, the most
painful is just being told

00:08:57.930 --> 00:08:59.253
you're too sensitive.

00:09:00.810 --> 00:09:04.620
And it hurts because it's the very thing

00:09:04.620 --> 00:09:07.710
that a sensitive person
would not wanna be told.

00:09:07.710 --> 00:09:11.370
It makes them feel like
they're not enough,

00:09:11.370 --> 00:09:12.540
they'll never be enough.

00:09:12.540 --> 00:09:14.190
No one will ever understand that.

00:09:16.059 --> 00:09:17.520
- Mm. Okay.

00:09:17.520 --> 00:09:19.200
I think, the most painful
thing I've been told

00:09:19.200 --> 00:09:24.123
is that I might never know
what this is all about.

00:09:25.020 --> 00:09:29.163
Yeah. That this life might
always be a mystery, for sure.

00:09:30.630 --> 00:09:31.463
- [Thoraya] Wait, before you go,

00:09:31.463 --> 00:09:34.740
have you gotten any answers
as you're going older?

00:09:34.740 --> 00:09:38.130
- Just opinions and none
of 'em are really answers,

00:09:38.130 --> 00:09:39.720
'cause no one really knows.

00:09:39.720 --> 00:09:41.670
- [Thoraya] What do you believe?

00:09:41.670 --> 00:09:44.223
- Take your time and
enjoy the little things.

00:09:45.210 --> 00:09:48.060
- The most painful thing I've been told

00:09:48.060 --> 00:09:50.130
was something I was told

00:09:50.130 --> 00:09:53.340
that I didn't even realize I was told,

00:09:53.340 --> 00:09:58.340
which is I was 45 and I got
diagnosed with bipolar disorder.

00:10:00.930 --> 00:10:01.920
I lived my whole life,

00:10:01.920 --> 00:10:04.770
two children, a wife, the house,

00:10:04.770 --> 00:10:07.650
San Diego, beautiful, everything great.

00:10:07.650 --> 00:10:09.960
And then, I lost it.

00:10:09.960 --> 00:10:12.900
I lived on the street, I
lived on the street in Mexico.

00:10:12.900 --> 00:10:15.660
I went to jail five times in Mexico.

00:10:15.660 --> 00:10:19.863
And then, because of my sister,
the only one that saved me.

00:10:25.093 --> 00:10:27.030
She saved me

00:10:27.030 --> 00:10:29.100
and brought me in and
I'm living in her place.

00:10:29.100 --> 00:10:32.253
- [Thoraya] What was the
most hurtful part of it all?

00:10:33.090 --> 00:10:34.113
- Oh, my kids.

00:10:36.150 --> 00:10:36.983
I was

00:10:37.860 --> 00:10:38.763
the go-to.

00:10:40.410 --> 00:10:42.690
The wife owned an advertising agency.

00:10:42.690 --> 00:10:45.090
She's lovely, she's
awesome, but she's a worker.

00:10:47.817 --> 00:10:51.099
I worked from home and I had the kids.

00:10:51.099 --> 00:10:56.010
And they were my babies and
I just disappeared on 'em.

00:10:56.010 --> 00:10:59.820
And I was, every day at school,

00:10:59.820 --> 00:11:01.140
everything, every soccer,

00:11:01.140 --> 00:11:04.950
doing gymnastics in the
backyard, everything.

00:11:04.950 --> 00:11:07.980
And then, I was gone and
there was a babysitter

00:11:07.980 --> 00:11:12.733
and boy, let me tell you,
that didn't help them at all.

00:11:14.100 --> 00:11:16.803
That was hardest thing, the hardest.

00:11:17.820 --> 00:11:19.890
I'm still feeling the effects.

00:11:19.890 --> 00:11:23.708
I just wanna say that I'm
in touch with my daughter

00:11:23.708 --> 00:11:25.914
- Mm-hmm.
- all the time,

00:11:25.914 --> 00:11:27.543
and we're starting to patch up.

00:11:28.440 --> 00:11:31.620
And I see my son three times a week.

00:11:31.620 --> 00:11:33.930
And I'm working on a product now,

00:11:33.930 --> 00:11:36.543
a golf product that I hope saves me.

00:11:38.160 --> 00:11:41.970
And it was a golf product
that me and my dad worked on

00:11:41.970 --> 00:11:43.950
and we worked on it together together.

00:11:43.950 --> 00:11:47.820
And then, he died and I
bailed out on it, of course.

00:11:47.820 --> 00:11:48.690
But now, I'm back.

00:11:48.690 --> 00:11:52.719
So, I feel like it's a gift
from my dad who is in heaven.

00:11:52.719 --> 00:11:55.830
What the product does
that nothing else does

00:11:55.830 --> 00:11:59.230
is it provides a clubface angle

00:12:00.840 --> 00:12:01.893
visibility,

00:12:03.120 --> 00:12:04.860
and it says if you're clubface

00:12:04.860 --> 00:12:08.880
and your putter path both
are square and on line,

00:12:08.880 --> 00:12:11.280
it uses a fused color,

00:12:11.280 --> 00:12:14.490
a blue color over a yellow
color that makes it green.

00:12:14.490 --> 00:12:16.200
And when it's green, you know it's good.

00:12:16.200 --> 00:12:19.590
I am selling it on fuzion.golf.

00:12:19.590 --> 00:12:20.970
It's ready to go right now.

00:12:20.970 --> 00:12:21.840
- [Thoraya] Okay, it'll be linked

00:12:21.840 --> 00:12:23.910
in the description for my listeners.

00:12:23.910 --> 00:12:24.743
Check it out.

00:12:24.743 --> 00:12:26.220
- Oh.
- There you go.

00:12:26.220 --> 00:12:27.900
Thank you so much.
- Any golfers out there?

00:12:27.900 --> 00:12:29.571
It works, I promise.

00:12:29.571 --> 00:12:32.644
Really good. Really, you'll be happy.

